# Running Dev Gates

Use the target Registry Stack checkout. Paths below are relative to its root.

## Select the checks

Start with the changed behavior and the smallest test that can expose a wrong
result. Add the owning contract or workflow check and any affected consumers.
Let protected CI supply the broad regression suite unless the change crosses
product boundaries, changes the gate itself, or CI cannot provide that proof.

Use these live sources instead of a copied job inventory:

| Concern | Source of truth |
|---|---|
| Changed-path ownership and reverse dependencies | `.github/scripts/ci_changes.py` and `.github/scripts/test_ci_changes.py` |
| Commands, feature flags, services, and aggregate results | `.github/workflows/ci.yml` and the affected standalone workflow |
| Package test/clippy invocation | `.github/scripts/run_cargo_packages.py` |
| Evidence, including wallet delivery | `products/evidence/scripts/` and the relevant `crates/registry-evidence*/tests/` |
| Discovery index and client handoff | `products/discovery/scripts/` |
| Base Registry Engine contracts, PostgreSQL, and adopter workflow | `products/breg/scripts/` |
| Casework review, tasks and source composition | `products/casework/AGENTS.md`, `products/casework/README.md`, and `products/casework/scripts/` |
| Shared Review selection and accepted binding | `crates/registry-review-protocol/README.md`, `crates/registry-review-client/tests/http_boundary.rs`, and affected provider tests |
| Coordinator authoring, admission, waits and recovery | `products/coordinator/AGENTS.md`, `products/coordinator/README.md`, and `products/coordinator/scripts/` |
| Messaging adapters, dispatch and delivery receipts | `products/messaging/AGENTS.md`, `products/messaging/scripts/`, and the relevant `crates/registry-messaging/tests/` |
| Scheduling capacity and task-grant commits | `products/scheduling/AGENTS.md`, `products/scheduling/TASK_GRANTS.md`, and `crates/registry-scheduling/tests/` |
| Render input hashing, deterministic output and serving | `products/render/PAYLOAD.md`, `products/render/ACCEPTANCE.md`, and `crates/registry-render/tests/` |
| Platform features, hygiene, and fixtures | `products/platform/` and the selected platform jobs in `ci.yml` |
| Identifiers and Registry Record | `products/identifiers/scripts/` and `products/registry-record/scripts/` |
| Language bindings and unified client packaging | The binding jobs in `ci.yml`, owning package metadata, and `release/scripts/client_registry.py` |
| Documentation and executable tutorials | `docs/site/AGENTS.md`, `docs/site/package.json`, the selected tutorial scripts, and any crate test that reads the page through `include_str!` |
| Release identity, packaging, and publication | `release/OPERATIONS.md` and the affected `release/scripts/test_*.py` |

PR checks are path-selected. A green result proves the selected jobs, not an
unselected boundary. When adding or moving a crate, contract, tutorial, or
generated input, inspect the classifier's ownership and update its tests if
selection must change. Execute the affected gate as well as checking its route.
A failed `Changed paths` job skips every path-selected job, so read it first;
a run with few failures may be a run that selected nothing. Workflow files do
not establish the live branch-protection required-check list.

## Local execution

For a Rust behavior change, use the owning package and focused test target:

```bash
cargo fmt --check
cargo test --locked -p <package> --test <test-target>
cargo clippy --locked -p <package> --all-targets -- -D warnings
```

Select required features from the owning workflow. Preserve the workspace's
