# yaml-language-server: $schema=https://id.registrystack.org/schemas/adapter/pack/pack.v1alpha1.schema.json
#
# The kobotoolbox pack: KoboToolbox submission acquisition for the
# governed-ingestion job mode, one source route, one page per run
# (CONCEPT 17.1 and 17.2). Unproved state, stated plainly: no KoboToolbox
# server has been reached. Every upstream shape here is synthesized from
# the published documentation, and every fixture beside this pack is
# synthetic and `documented`, never `captured`. `testedVersions` is
# empty on purpose: it lists versions a pack was exercised against, and
# none was. The hosted KoboToolbox documentation carries no server
# version, so there is no honest version list to write; the acceptance
# row of CONCEPT 17.7 lists every behavior resting on documentation as
# unproved, and the pack README carries the probe questions.
#
# What the pack covers: the v2 submissions listing, `GET
# /api/v2/assets/{uid}/data/` (the v1 `/submissions/` name was renamed
# to `data` in v2; kobotoolbox/docs source/migrating_api.md, published
# from https://support.kobotoolbox.org/api.html). One route,
# `kobo-submissions`: one page per run, `limit` fixed at 100 (the
# documented default page size; a pack never raises a server bound),
# `start` from the job cursor. The reply envelope is
# `{count, next, previous, results}`; the route reads `results` only and
# never follows the reply's `next` URL, because the cursor is this
# pack's own `{offset}` object and paging stays origin-pinned by
# construction.
#
# Deployment scoping: the asset (form) a job reads is a deployment
# value, and a source route carries no template parameters. The
# deployment-owned slot is the endpoint binding's `baseUrl`: the engine
# pins the origin plus its base path (CONCEPT 8.11.5) and every send
# stays under it, so the runtime config binds `kobo-api` to the data
# URL of the deployment's own asset (see
# products/adapter/examples/kobotoolbox-job/runtime.example.yaml) and
# this pack sends `path: /`, which lands on the documented trailing
# slash. If the job compiler grows a parameters block on the job
# definition, these bindings should move there.
#
# Authentication (cited choice): KoboToolbox API requests authenticate
# with an API token over `Authorization: Token <token>`
# (kobotoolbox/docs source/migrating_api.md) or with Basic auth over
# TLS (the same documentation retrieves the token with
# `curl -u username:password`). An endpoint declares one kind, so this
# pack declares `basic`; a deployment that prefers the token swaps the
# kind to `static-authorization` with `scheme: Token` and binds
# tokenRef in the runtime config. Both sides of the kind match must
# move together. The endpoint declares no request or response header
# allowlists: the documented data read consumes no header the engine
# would copy, so the engine sends and copies nothing beyond its own.
#
# Item mapping (probe-gated, see the pack README): key = `_id` as
# text, revision = `_uuid`, value = the submission object as returned.
# `_validation_status` never appears in any step; it may pass through
# only inside `value`. No write, patch, or delete endpoint exists in
# this pack.
#
# Error clauses: the 401 answer never reaches the route - the engine's
# authentication plan raises the uncatchable `credential.rejected` for
# a refused Basic credential - so the pack adds no clause for it. The
# transport faults redeliver once, like the dhis2-tracker reads; a GET
# is safe to repeat. Every other error propagates as its own class.
apiVersion: id.registrystack.org/formats/adapter/pack/v1alpha1
kind: AdapterPack
id: kobotoolbox
version: "1"
testedVersions: []
endpoints:
  - id: kobo-api
    component: http
    authentication:
      type: basic
    attemptTimeoutMilliseconds: 10000
    maximumResponseBytes: 1048576
    operations:
      - id: submissions-page
    testedVersions: []
sourceRoutes:
  - id: kobo-submissions
    scan: ongoing
    nextRecovery: key-deduplicated
    steps:
      - onException:
          exception:
            - upstream.timeout
            - upstream.connection
          redeliveryPolicy:
            maximumRedeliveries: 1
            retryDelaySeconds: 2
      # The offset this run fetches: the engine restores the job cursor
      # into the AdapterJobCursor property, absent on the first run
      # (CONCEPT 17.2); scripts/seed-offset.rhai turns that into the
      # Kobo `start` value.
