# Local proof by regression test

Turn one testable finding into an oracle that asserts safe behavior, run
it, and record `POC-RESULTS.md` and `POC-RESULTS.json`. Accept a finding or
findings path plus `--repo`, `--id`, `--post-fix`, `--keep`, and `--fresh`.

Read [the workflow](references/workflow.md) for selection, isolated test
authoring, checkpoint schemas, commands, verdicts, cleanup, and redaction.

- Execute only an owned, trusted local checkout. Cargo compilation also
  runs build scripts and proc macros; offline mode is not a sandbox for
  unknown third-party code. State a blocker if this trust requirement fails.
- Use existing fixtures, fabricated credentials, deterministic inputs,
  and loopback-only services. No live sources or external targets.
- Start with one `cargo test --locked --offline` oracle. Missing cached
  dependencies or a build error is inconclusive, not proof or refutation.
  Verify that the named oracle actually executed; zero or ignored tests
  cannot establish a pass. Run an ignored demonstration test explicitly.
  Run broader checks only when a retained test/fix or repository gate needs them.
- Record the command, assertion, exit, source state, and oracle hash.
  A post-fix pass alone proves only that this oracle passes now. Claim an
  observed fail-to-pass transition only with a matching recorded pre-fix
  assertion failure. Never weaken the oracle to get a pass.
- Never overwrite or remove an existing user test. Default cleanup removes
  only this run's unchanged temporary file; `--keep` retains it.
- Preserve helper guards, checkpointing, and redaction. Registry Stack
  reports/state belong in `registry-internal`; tests live in the owning crate.

