   366	satisfies it. Do not open a missing-sign-off finding; check the job's result
   367	instead of re-deriving it from the diff. If a finding cites a commit, cite one
   368	that still resolves in the pull request, not a rewritten or squashed SHA.
   369	
   370	## Rules that bite
   371	
   372	- Every commit needs a DCO sign-off: `git commit -s`.
   373	- Commit subjects: imperative mood; `feat(breg):` and `feat(evidence):` style
   374	  prefixes are the norm for product-scoped changes.
   375	- History may be rewritten during review (session commits get squashed). In
